<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugo Feb trade gap $113 mln vs $191 mln in Jan.</title>
<headline>Yugo Feb trade gap $113 mln vs $191 mln in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV TRADE     FEB 97     JAN 97	 FEB 96</p>
<p> Exports million USD  139	  132	    97</p>
<p> Imports		  252	  323	   212</p>
<p> Balance		 -113	 -191	  -115</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE FIGURES (JAN/FEB 97)</p>
<p> Exports million USD	283</p>
<p> Imports			634</p>
<p> Balance		     -351</p>
<p>NOTES - February 1997 exports rose 42.8 percent on February 1996, while imports rose 18.9 percent over the same period.</p>
<p>Data refer to the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>Yugoslavia ended 1996 with a $2.26 billion trade deficit -- Gordana Filipovic, Belgrade newsroom, +381 11 222 4254</p>
